Issue: The harness's own skill tells the agent to search the memory when the delivered examples do not cover the question, and the only way to search it is to read the frozen memory file raw. On the parent's traces 29 of its 60 USPTO samples and 3 of its 100 Symptom2Disease samples read `/harness/memory/memory.json`, 52,344-69,224 characters per read and 2,188,911 characters of raw JSON in the USPTO tool results alone, and every read re-delivers cases `retrieve_examples` has already handed the agent in compact form `[[/workspace/runs/83ed278ac33df92c592b4c5f3d6a1ca0170aab56/USPTO/conversations/0001/sample-1.json]]` `[[/workspace/runs/83ed278ac33df92c592b4c5f3d6a1ca0170aab56/results/samples.jsonl]]`. The reads bought nothing measurable: across the five runs whose evidence is byte-identical the samples that read the memory scored 23/141 (16.3%) against 28/118 (23.7%) for the samples that answered from the tool's evidence, and within one question -- one sample searching, its sibling not -- the pair is 6-4 over 70 pairs. They also sit where the memory has least to add: the tool's evidence already carries all 50 of USPTO's cases (8,663 characters) and 170.7 of Symptom2Disease's 200, while LawBench, whose evidence shows 53.8 of its 200 cases, searched in 0 of 100 samples in the parent and in this run.

Modification: the memory is exposed as a search the agent writes itself. `retrieval.search` answers the agent's own query with the memory's closest cases, through the same ranking and the same compact Q/A rendering the tool uses for the problem, inside a budget of its own (12,000 characters) and under a first line that says how many of the memory's cases the slice shows; `make_search_tool` registers it as `search_memory` and the tool registry adds the factory, so the agent asks the memory a question in its own words instead of reading a raw file. `retrieve_examples`, `render`, the memory, `prepare_memory.py`, the prompt's answer rules, `resolution`, `recovery`, `adjudication` and the answer-space rules are untouched, and no dataset name, label list or task branch appears in the code.

Results: {"scores": {"USPTO": 0.1833, "Symptom2Disease": 0.88, "LawBench": 0.61, "average": 0.5578, "status": "ok"}, "message": "The expected effect was achieved on the behaviour the mechanism was aimed at, and not on the score. Activation: 42 of 260 samples called `search_memory` (33 USPTO, 7 Symptom2Disease, 2 LawBench) for 93 calls, with the aspect queries the mechanism was built for -- `Functional group addition FGA CBr methyl bromination NBS precursor` (USPTO example 0 sample 1), `盗割正在使用中的公共照明电线 危害公共安全 罪名` (LawBench example 3 sample 0), `nausea chest pain shiver anxious` (Symptom2Disease example 7 sample 0) -- and the raw-file path is gone: 0 of 260 samples read the memory file against 32 of the parent's 260. The mechanism's own samples are 39 unchanged, 2 wrong->right (USPTO example 0 sample 1 and example 1 sample 1) and 1 right->wrong (example 16 sample 1) against the parent, and the 14 same-question pairs where exactly one sample searched all agree, so the +0.0211 is draw on the tasks and samples the tool did not decide and cannot be credited to it. The evidence and the answer path are provably unchanged (245/245 byte-identical `retrieve_examples` outputs, memories byte-identical to the parent's, 28 answer-path fixes / 0 breaks). Cost: 3 USPTO samples repeated the same two searches 21-22 times (1.35-1.45 M input tokens each, 293-307 s, all three wrong), which is 32% of the run's tokens; outside them the task is cheaper per call than the parent."}

